# ── yt-pipeline cron example ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Edit paths, then:  crontab -e  (or drop into /etc/cron.d/)
#
# Daily at 15:00 UTC — fully unattended (render + upload, approval gate skipped):
0 15 * * *  cd /home/user/yt-pipeline && /usr/bin/python3 run.py run --auto >> output/cron.log 2>&1
#
# Twice daily, only render (review manually with `python run.py list` + `approve`):
# 0 9,21 * * *  cd /home/user/yt-pipeline && /usr/bin/python3 run.py run --no-upload >> output/cron.log 2>&1
